          ":question/id": "5c16e54f-5eb3-5538-b6ef-5278b1d8b5d6",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ x+2y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
