          ":question/id": "a097e129-49a9-557e-ae8d-2bc55f77bbbd",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-3z &=4 \\\\ x-y-4z &=7 \\\\ -2x+2y+7z &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
