        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "015dbcb1-9cd9-5627-aca2-4098742f5e7e",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z &=-1 \\\\ 2x+5y-9z &=0 \\\\ 2x+6y-12z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -12 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -12 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -12 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/id": "4eaacc27-98c5-59a8-8685-f364173f3d7b",
              ":answer-field/key": "I",
              ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
