        "knowledge_point": {
          "db_id": 17592186115299,
          "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
          "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "be801b20-0dc9-589e-a38c-ed3285e40dd4",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y &=3 \\\\ 4x-8y &=7 \\\\ 2x+2y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
