        "question": {
          ":question/id": "5c2b0374-da4b-5875-b2ca-1a9f0e5275de",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y &=-3 \\\\ -4x+8y &=-6 \\\\ 6x-12y &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution",
          ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 6 & -12 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 6 & -12 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -12 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
